# Project log maintenance

- Before work, read `PROJECT_LOG.md` (or the linked canonical equivalent) and the current repository reference.
- At material boundaries, update the local log and affected status/profile/checklist, then route a sanitized central History update through the owner when History is open.
- Record event time, observation time, component/change, reason, result/verification, source reference, next action, and unresolved/removed/deferred work.
- Never record secrets, credentials, raw infrastructure output, private cross-project backlinks, or inferred test/deploy success.
- Do not create per-tool-call entries, recursive log-only commits, forced rewrites, or unrelated feature/service/database/deployment changes.
